#N canvas 0 50 1040 910 12;
#X text 30 16 =^..^=   smear~   version 1 (2026)   sofia vallejo budziszewski   iem kug graz austria;
#X text 30 46 spectral smear;
#X text 30 86 blurs the spectrum over time and over frequency so short sounds turn into long washes, f 110;
#X text 30 126 --- how it was made ---;
#X text 30 170 the same stft engine. the magnitude of every bin is averaged over time (or the peaks are held) and blurred over neighbouring bins. the phase is kept or randomised, f 110;
#X text 30 230 --- how to use ---;
#X text 30 274 1  open the engine page and switch the sound on, f 110;
#X text 30 304 2  increase time to make the tail longer, f 110;
#X text 30 334 3  shape toward 1 holds the loudest moments and gives the longest tails, f 110;
#X text 30 364 everything is a message: see the messages page for the full list and the examples page for patches to copy. every effect has presets and a and b morph and mutate and a data inlet, f 110;
#X text 30 424 try:  short time values give reverb-like blur. long values give pads, f 110;
#X text 30 454 try:  width blurs across frequency and makes the sound more noisy, f 110;
#X text 30 498 --- common problems ---;
#X text 30 542 no sound: check mix and that dsp is on, f 110;
#X text 30 572 very quiet: shape near 0 averages the sound and lowers the level. raise shape, f 110;
#X text 30 602 names: give every instance its own name as the first argument like [tessera/smear~ s1]. the name is also the stash namespace, f 110;
#X text 30 666 --- click a box to open that page ---;
#N canvas 0 50 900 1026 presets 0;
#X text 30 16 factory sounds are stored as plain text. click a box to load that sound. every slider in the effect follows, f 100;
#X text 30 66 --- factory presets ---;
#X msg 30 110 \; s1 preset 0;
#X text 240 112 0  default;
#X msg 30 164 \; s1 preset 1;
#X text 240 166 1  soft wash;
#X msg 30 218 \; s1 preset 2;
#X text 240 220 2  long tail;
#X msg 460 110 \; s1 preset 3;
#X text 670 112 3  blur;
#X msg 460 164 \; s1 preset 4;
#X text 670 166 4  noise bed;
#X msg 460 218 \; s1 preset 5;
#X text 670 220 5  subtle;
#X text 30 292 --- now playing ---;
#X symbolatom 30 336 20 0 0 0 - s1-name -;
#X floatatom 230 336 4 0 0 0 - s1-index -;
#X text 340 338 name and number (minus one means edited);
#X msg 30 380 \; s1 next;
#X msg 142 380 \; s1 prev;
#X msg 254 380 \; s1 mutate 0.3;
#X text 30 440 next and prev step through the presets and wrap around. mutate varies the current sound by a random amount from 0 to 1. mutate leaves mix and level alone, f 100;
#X text 30 490 --- morph between two sounds ---;
#X msg 30 534 \; s1 A;
#X msg 118 534 \; s1 B;
#X text 206 536 a and b remember the current sound;
#X text 30 596 morph;
#X obj 110 594 hsl 300 18 0 1 0 0 s1-morph empty empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 30 638 load one preset and press a then load another and press b then move the morph slider. every continuous parameter blends smoothly. switches change at the middle, f 100;
#X text 30 688 --- your own user bank ---;
#X msg 30 732 \; s1 store mysound;
#X msg 214 732 \; s1 save my.bank;
#X msg 390 732 \; s1 load my.bank;
#X text 30 792 store keeps the current sound after the factory presets. save writes the user bank to a text file next to this patch and load reads such a file, f 100;
#X text 30 842 --- presets with stash ---;
#X text 30 886 every slider of the effect sends to s1-param and listens on s1-param-r. this is the naming scheme of the stash preset library: create [stash/bank s1] and send it a scan message with the name of the patch that holds the effect. it follows the stash rules but has not been tested together yet, f 100;
#X restore 30 710 pd presets;
#X text 30 744 all sounds and morph, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1200 410 parameters 0;
#X text 30 16 every parameter is also a message: [name value( in real units or for a switch the option name or number. the controls in the effect panel and these messages do the same, f 120;
#X text 30 66 parameter;
#X text 210 66 values;
#X text 560 66 what it does;
#X text 30 100 time;
#X text 210 100 1 to 4000 log, f 36;
#X text 560 100 how long a sound keeps ringing in ms, f 54;
#X text 30 136 shape;
#X text 210 136 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 136 0 averages over time and 1 holds the loudest moments, f 54;
#X text 30 192 width;
#X text 210 192 1 to 64, f 36;
#X text 560 192 blur across neighbouring bins, f 54;
#X text 30 228 diffuse;
#X text 210 228 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 228 random phase that turns held tones into noise, f 54;
#X text 30 264 mix;
#X text 210 264 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 264 0 is the dry sound and 1 is only the effect, f 54;
#X text 30 310 any continuous parameter can be driven by data: send datamap name amount and then data 0 to 1. see the messages page, f 120;
#X restore 220 710 pd parameters;
#X text 220 744 every control, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1300 1088 messages 0;
#X text 30 16 click any box to send it to the effect. the effect listens to its name so you can use [s s1] from anywhere in your patch, f 110;
#X text 30 66 message;
#X text 430 66 what it does;
#X msg 30 100 \; s1 params;
#X text 430 102 prints every parameter and its range in the console, f 76;
#X msg 30 154 \; s1 preset 3;
#X text 430 156 loads preset 3 (or a preset by name: preset soft wash), f 76;
#X msg 30 208 \; s1 next;
#X text 430 210 next preset (wraps around), f 76;
#X msg 30 262 \; s1 prev;
#X text 430 264 previous preset, f 76;
#X msg 30 316 \; s1 mutate 0.4;
#X text 430 318 random variation of the current sound. 0 is nothing and 1 is a lot, f 76;
#X msg 30 370 \; s1 A;
#X text 430 372 remember the current sound as a, f 76;
#X msg 30 424 \; s1 B;
#X text 430 426 remember the current sound as b, f 76;
#X msg 30 478 \; s1 morph 0.5;
#X text 430 480 blend between a and b from 0 to 1, f 76;
#X msg 30 532 \; s1 data 0.7;
#X text 430 534 data inlet: a value from 0 to 1, f 76;
#X msg 30 586 \; s1 datamap time 0.5;
#X text 430 588 map the data inlet to a continuous parameter. 0.5 means the full range of the parameter at data 0 and 1. amount 0 removes the mapping. up to four mappings, f 76;
#X msg 30 660 \; s1 datamap clear;
#X text 430 662 remove all data mappings, f 76;
#X msg 30 714 \; s1 store mysound;
#X text 430 716 keep the current sound in the user bank, f 76;
#X msg 30 768 \; s1 save my.bank;
#X text 430 770 write the user bank to a text file, f 76;
#X msg 30 822 \; s1 load my.bank;
#X text 430 824 read a user bank, f 76;
#X msg 30 876 \; s1 size 4096;
#X text 430 878 fft size 256 to 16384 (latency equals the size), f 76;
#X msg 30 930 \; s1 reset;
#X text 430 932 clears the buffers, f 76;
#X msg 30 984 \; s1 latency;
#X text 430 986 prints the delay in the console, f 76;
#X restore 410 710 pd messages;
#X text 410 744 clickable list, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1300 1000 examples 0;
#X text 30 16 copy these into your own patch. they all talk to the effect through [s s1] so the engine page must be open with dsp on, f 130;
#X text 30 56 1  walk through the presets;
#X obj 30 90 tgl 18 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X obj 30 130 metro 2500;
#X obj 30 170 random 6;
#X obj 30 210 list prepend preset;
#X obj 30 250 list trim;
#X obj 30 290 s s1;
#X text 330 56 2  slow morph between preset 0 and 1;
#X msg 330 90 \; s1 preset 0 \; s1 A \; s1 preset 1 \; s1 B;
#X obj 330 210 tgl 18 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X obj 330 250 metro 6000;
#X msg 330 290 0 \, 1 3000 \, 0 3000 3000;
#X obj 330 330 line 0 30;
#X obj 330 370 list prepend morph;
#X obj 330 410 list trim;
#X obj 330 450 s s1;
#X text 740 56 3  sweep time with a ramp;
#X obj 740 90 tgl 18 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X obj 740 130 metro 4000;
#X msg 740 170 50 \, 3000 2000 \, 50 2000 2000;
#X obj 740 210 line 50 30;
#X obj 740 250 list prepend time;
#X obj 740 290 list trim;
#X obj 740 330 s s1;
#X text 30 556 4  data in: a ramp stands in for a sensor or a csv column. click the map box once first;
#X msg 30 590 \; s1 datamap time 0.4;
#X obj 30 650 tgl 18 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X obj 30 690 metro 4000;
#X msg 30 730 0 \, 1 2000 \, 0 2000 2000;
#X obj 30 770 line 0 30;
#X obj 30 810 list prepend data;
#X obj 30 850 list trim;
#X obj 30 890 s s1;
#X text 330 650 in your own patch send any value from 0 to 1 to [s s1] as: data 0.7. for a csv series scale it to the range 0 to 1 first. [tessera/datamod~] does that for you and its data outlet can be connected straight to the inlet of any tessera effect, f 70;
